# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ninesixteen.video — desktop app environment (Vite)
#
# Setup:
#   1. Copy this file to `.env` in this same folder:
#        cp .env.example .env
#   2. Fill in the values below (same Firebase client config as apps/web).
#   3. For release builds, env is baked in at build time — set `.env` BEFORE:
#        pnpm desktop:build
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the app.
# When Firebase vars are blank, dev runs in demo mode (local fake account).
# Production builds REQUIRE all VITE_FIREBASE_* vars to be set.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Firebase (client) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Firebase Console → Project settings → General → Your apps (Web).
# Use the SAME values as NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_* in apps/web/.env.local
# so sign-in, uid, and Pro entitlement are shared with the website.
#
# Authentication → Sign-in method: enable Google + Email/Password.
#
# If email/password sign-in fails in the release app with "Failed to fetch",
# check Google Cloud → Credentials → your API key → Application restrictions.
# Add HTTP referrers:
#   https://tauri.localhost/*
#   http://localhost:1420/*
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ── Web app URL ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL of the Next.js site. Used when the desktop app:
#   • Opens Google sign-in in the browser (auth handoff back to the app)
#   • Opens Stripe checkout / billing in the browser
#   • Opens Terms / Privacy links
#
# Local dev (web on port 3000):
#   VITE_WEB_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Production:
#   VITE_WEB_URL=https://ninesixteen.video
VITE_WEB_URL=https://ninesixteen.video

# ── Optional: release debugging (runtime — not read from this file) ─
# Attach a console + backtraces when running the built .exe (PowerShell):
#   $env:NINESIXTEEN_DEBUG = "1"
#   & ".\apps\desktop\src-tauri\target\release\ninesixteen.exe"
#
# Logs always go to: %USERPROFILE%\Videos\ninesixteen\ninesixteen.log
